## Cause

The acceptance result `phase-acceptance-p2-571d8779.json` holds finding F1: GREEN_TEST_COMMAND fails 1 test, D6 of
`dashboard/__tests__/quest-cover-f3f6.test.ts`. For the week 6 reader "Tap, Tap!" in the workbook output, the art
source of page 1 is `l2-w06-cover-tap-tap-hair-v1.png`, and the pin held `l2-w06-cover-tap-tap-line-v1.png`.

Commit e0350881 of track storytime_print_r1_20261025 (2026-11-14, the r6-v2 fix batch, decision D7 hair fill) added
`content/storytime/l2/print/pictures-line-fix.json`. Its entry `l2-w06-cover-tap-tap` maps the source file
`l2-w06-cover-tap-tap-line-v1.png` to the replacement `l2/print/pictures-fix/l2-w06-cover-tap-tap-hair-v1.png`. The
build applies the table through `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/line-art-fix.ts`.

Orchestrator decision: the D6 pin follows the fix table. The approved D7 replacement is the intended art. The cover
code does not change.

## The one edit

File: `dashboard/__tests__/quest-cover-f3f6.test.ts`, test D6 (final mode, both outputs).

- New import: `readStorytimeLineArtFixTable` from `../lib/storytime/print/line-art-fix`.
- The table is read one time per test: `const fixTable = readStorytimeLineArtFixTable();`.
- The former `else if` branch is now an `else` branch. For the `workbook` output, when the table holds an entry whose
  `sourceFile` equals `wantedFile`, the pinned file name is `path.basename(entry.replacement)`. Else it stays
  `wantedFile`. The problem message keeps its form and names the pinned file.
- The comment of the change is above it, with the date 2026-11-18, the acceptance F1, and the orchestrator decision.

SHA-256 of the edited test file: `09d7c4bc8f2869e029c840031501318a8eac85cca72ed3b58e509756f222b764`.

No other test and no code file changed. `pnpm install` did not run.

